    {
      "id": "n5-u02-g02",
      "title": "この・その・あの・どの + noun",
      "pattern": "この / その / あの / どの + N",
      "meaning": "this N / that N / that N over there / which N",
      "explanation": "この, その, あの and どの work like これ, それ, あれ and どれ, but they must be followed by a noun. この本 means \"this book\" and あの人 means \"that person over there\". Compare: これは本です (This is a book) and この本は私の本です (This book is my book). Think of the の at the end as a hook that grabs the next noun.",
      "notes": [
        "Never use この / その / あの / どの alone: × このは本です.",
        "あの人 (that person) is very common; あの方 is the polite version."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "jp": "この傘[かさ]は私[わたし]の傘[かさ]です。",
          "en": "This umbrella is my umbrella."
        },
