    {
      "id": "n5-u02-g03",
      "title": "何・だれ — what? who?",
      "pattern": "N は 何 / だれ ですか",
      "meaning": "What / who is N?",
      "explanation": "何 means \"what\" and だれ means \"who\". Put the question word exactly where the answer would go and add か at the end — the word order does not change. だれの means \"whose\": だれのかばんですか = Whose bag is it? 何の + noun asks \"what kind of\": 何の本ですか = What kind of book is it?",
      "notes": [
        "何 is read なん before です, の and counters, and なに in most other places.",
        "どなた is a polite version of だれ; use it about people you respect.",
        "Never use 何 to ask about a person: ask あの人はだれですか."
