      "title": "の — \"mine, yours, Ken's\"",
      "pattern": "N の です",
      "meaning": "It's N's (one)",
      "explanation": "When everyone already knows which thing you mean, you can drop the noun after の. この傘は私のです means \"This umbrella is mine.\" To ask who owns something, say だれのですか — \"Whose is it?\" This saves you from repeating the same noun twice.",
